// name :
"P2803746010" "The Price for Fire"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - PandorasBoxVillainArc4Souvenir 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef Name :
"P2200856068" "A Blade of Bronze"
// tDetailString :
"P3443711298" "This polished metal blade no longer shines with cosmic energy, as it did when a Pandora entity cut into Doctor Harvan with it. After everything you've been through, in fighting to claim the power from Pandora's Box, you can't help but wonder if all this conflict was the original goal of the Incarnate Zeus. All of this conflict and mayhem may simply be...<br><br><b><color gold>The Price for Fire</color></b><br><br>Your troubles began when Doctor Harvan came to you with a plan to recapture the power released from Pandora's Box. You went to your mobile base, the U.S.S. Mitscher, to retrieve the Antikythera. When you arrived, however, you found the ship under attack. Arachnos had discovered the Mitscher's location, and had stolen the Antikythera. You fought off the remaining soldiers and spoke with Lastri, who believed that Captain Mako might have betrayed you.<br><br>You went straight to Grandville, the heart of the Isles, to confront Mako in person. Bemused by your boldness and seeking to retain your trust, Mako informed you that Black Scorpion was involved in the attack on the Mitscher. He even accompanied you for an assault on Black Scorpion's base, though you got the feeling he had other, more personal motives for doing so.<br><br>Together, you and Mako retrieved the Antikythera, and you brought it back to Doctor Harvan. Harvan led you to his lab, which he claimed had been built based on designs his father had left behind. Harvan activated the device inside, which began to draw in the released energies of Pandora's Box.<br><br>Unfortunately, the Pandora entities that had attacked you earlier arrived as well, and you had to fight off a swarm of golden beings. Just as the device finished its process, Harvan was cut down by an errant attack. You moved to his aid, but Harvan was acting strangely - his speech was muffled by the whirring sounds of broken machinery.<br><br>It was at that moment you realized the truth: James Harvan was an automaton, an artificial creation intended to appear human. Nemesis revealed himself to you, reveling in his plan's success. He then began to empower his automatons with the energy from Pandora's Box, and sent them to destroy you. You escaped intact, but it appears that Nemesis is now in possession of a power of mythical proportions. Who knows what he might have planned..."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - LastriTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page TaskIncomplete Text :
"P10878801" "<color orange>Lastri is gritting her teeth in frustration. After a moment, she takes a short breath, stands tall, and meets your gaze.</color><br><br>{Hero.gender=male Sir|Ma'am}, I must apologize. I assured you that I would take care of the Mitscher, and that my men could staff and defend it if necessary. As you can see, we failed to defend the Mitscher from attack. I claim full responsibility."
// Answer Text :
"P1623321453" "Where is the Antikythera, Lastri?"
// Page Lastri1 Text :
"P1469535254" "<color orange>Lastri flinches at the mention of the Antikythera. She averts her eyes in shame.</color><br><br>The Antikythera was their target, {HeroName}. Once they had taken the Mitscher, Arachnos tore through every cargo hold in the ship. I... I believe they have taken it, {Hero.gender=male sir|ma'am}."
// Answer Text :
"P775701634" "How did they manage to find the Mitscher?"
// Answer Text :
"P2530906923" "Hmph. I knew you couldn't be trusted."
// Page Betrayal Text :
"P887482243" "{HeroName}! {Hero.gender=male Sir|Ma'am}, I...<br><br><color orange>Lastri cuts herself off momentarily, lips tight. She puts her hand to her forehead for a moment. After calming herself, she continues.</color><br><br>{Hero.gender=male Sir|Ma'am}. I realize that I have not been forthcoming about my employer, or his motives. I apologize for this, but it remains a necessity. Anonymity is of paramount importance to him, and it is not something I can be flexible with.<br><br>However, I entered into a contract with you to establish a power base, to allow you to rival Arachnos for control over the Rogue Isles. And I intend to honor that contract. I can assure you, that despite this setback, we can <i>and will</i> recover. Allow me this chance to prove to you my intentions. You will <b><i>not</b></i> regret it."
// Answer Text :
"P491442480" "If you're not with Arachnos, how did they locate the ship?"
// Page Track Text :
"P2973581446" "Ever since Pandora's Box was opened, the Mitscher has been harried by the same creatures that attacked you underneath Zigursky Penitentiary. Doctor Harvan believes it is because of the presence of the Antikythera.<br><br>It is... <i>possible</i> that Arachnos managed to discover a way of tracking either them or whatever force is drawing them to the Antikythera. However...<br><br>The Antikythera itself is the only tool we know of capable of tracking and measuring energy signatures related to Pandora's Box. And even if we were to assume that Arachnos was in possession of such a device..."
// Answer Text :
"P23332987" "Then why would they need the Antikythera in the first place?"
// Page Track2 Text :
"P3622085448" "Yes, exactly. However... there is another explanation.<br><br><color orange>Lastri's cheeks begin to burn with shame again.</color><br><br>It is possible... that my once-over of the Arachnos Flier that Captain Mako donated to us was... not quite thorough enough. If that is the case, and the Flier was indeed bugged, it would have been a simple matter to set up an ambush like this.<br><br>Unfortunately, the Flier was Arachnos's first target when they appeared. Any attempt to verify my suspicions would involve a deep-sea salvage operation, I'm afraid."
// Answer Text :
"P389601770" "Mako. I should have known."
// Page Track3 Text :
"P3622999309" "I'll begin monitoring all internal Arachnos communications for mentions of the Antikythera or Pandora's Box. Within a few days, I should be able to-"
// Answer Text :
"P2926141907" "No, Lastri. I'll handle this personally."
// Page TeamTaskIncomplete SayOutLoudText :
"P812864542" "{Hero.gender=male Sir|Ma'am}, I must apologize. We failed to defend the Mitscher from attack."
// Page TeamLastri1 SayOutLoudText :
"P3350821353" "The Antikythera was their target. I believe they have taken it, {Hero.gender=male sir|ma'am}."
// Page TeamBetrayal SayOutLoudText :
"P2080423366" "{Hero.gender=male Sir|Ma'am}! I intend to honor our contract. Allow me this chance to prove to you my intentions."
// Page TeamTrack SayOutLoudText :
"P909289456" "It's possible that Arachnos managed to discover a way of tracking Pandora Energy. However... I don't believe that's likely."
// Page TeamTrack2 SayOutLoudText :
"P4046869479" "If the Flier was bugged, it would have been simple to set up an ambush like this. Unfortunately, we cannot verify this, as the Flier was destroyed."
// Page TeamTrack3 SayOutLoudText :
"P2508379432" "I'll begin monitoring Arachnos communications. Within a few days, I should be able to-"
// Page NotTaskOwner Text :
"P2620207394" "<color skyblue>Only the team leader can cause the mission to progress through dialogue."
// Answer Text :
"P4060782435" "Leave"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P856364347" ""
// SendOffString :
"P3698914903" "If we're going to try to harness the freed energy from Pandora's Box, we're going to need to use the one tool known to be capable of altering the Box's power emanations: the Antikythera.<br><br>Currently, I believe, Lastri has it stored aboard the U.S.S. Mitscher. We'll need to have it on-hand before we can make any progress towards harnessing the power of those creatures."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P68395324" "Retrieve the Antikythera"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P3542412469" "{HeroName}, we need the Antikythera before we can proceed. I'm afraid any attempts to corral the energy of Pandora's Box would be futile without it."
// TaskTitle :
"P3087706601" "<color deepskyblue>The Price for Fire</color>"
// TaskSubTitle :
"P2397423992" "<color deepskyblue>Part One: While the Iron is Hot</color>"

