// Script Variable RescueObjectiveText :
"P1798300379" "Rescue Lastri"
// Script Variable BOSS_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P45164572" "We've got what we need. Time to clean up."
// Script Variable BOSS_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P246405762" "Crap, there's a live one! Shoot to kill!"
// Script Variable CAPTOR_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P2234509129" "<t 2><t 0>This one's still moving. Do we bring her in for interrogation?"
// Script Variable WaveShout :
"P1936714319" "<shout>Stop {HeroName}!"
// Script Variable Greeting :
"P3609192693" "{HeroName}, it's you."
// BEHAVIORLIST :
"P1138006687" "<em stancehero1>"
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P892451606" "I die!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P4229670543" "You have fended off an Arachnos attack... but not before they could steal the Antikythera!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P502778460" "<color orange>Doctor Harvan pales visibly when you relate the events aboard the Mitscher to him.</color><br><br>This is very trying news, {HeroName}. Without the Antikythera, any attempt at controlling the energy released by Pandora's Box will be utterly futile. We need to retrieve it as quickly as possible.<br><br>We have time... I doubt Arachnos will be able to decode the Antikythera's readings without at least a few weeks of study. I daresay that they could kidnap the entire mainstream archaeological community and would not gain a single iota of usable knowledge."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Compound2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - MakoTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page TaskIncomplete Text :
"P2071415822" "<color orange>Captain Mako stiffens as you approach. He jerks his head to the side, indicating a corner for the two of you to talk. When he speaks, it is in a low, hushed tone.</color><br><br>Have you gone <i>insane</i>? What are you doing here? You're not exactly on the best terms with Recluse right now, {HeroName}. This is the last place you should be, and you <b><i>certainly</b></i> shouldn't be talking to me like this.<br><br>Kinda hard for me to play double agent if you're just going to walk up and have a chat. You're going to get yourself killed."
// Answer Text :
"P2419107997" "Can it, Mako. The Mitscher was attacked, and I want answers."
// Answer Text :
"P4236525034" "Perhaps the beating didn't make it clear. You people don't scare me."
// Page Hostile Text :
"P2870004557" "<color orange>Mako makes a face at you. It's hard to tell with sharks, but you <i>think</i> it's exasperation.</color><br><br>Calm down. No one's going to attack you here, {HeroName}. Cardinal rule. No infighting in the boss's house. Still, you've got some serious brass coming here, I'll give you that.<br><br>Now, I know you well enough to realize that you're <i>smarter</i> than this. You wouldn't risk exposing our little deal if you didn't have a reason, so you may as well have out with it."
// Answer Text :
"P2644571872" "The Mitscher was attacked, and the Antikythera is missing."
// Page Answers Text :
"P2571103650" "That sucks, {HeroName}, and I feel for you. I just don't know why you're bothering <i>me</i> about it."
// Answer Text :
"P2037558627" "Attacked by ARACHNOS. You bugged the flier, didn't you?"
// Page Answers2 Text :
"P3418022077" "<color orange>Mako flails and makes a series of hushing noises at the mention of the word 'flier'. He spares a glance at Ghost Widow, who returns his look with an icy stare.</color><br><br>Hey, {Hero.gender=male man|lady}, keep it down. I <i>really</i> don't need it getting out that I sent you a flier, okay?<br><br>Look, I didn't bug the thing. I didn't need to. If I'd wanted to find the Mitscher I would have just called your ladyfriend and set up an appointment.<br><br>But I'm not the one in charge of production of those things, ok? Scorpion is. I saw an opportunity to disrupt his operations and cement my deal with you at the same time, so I took it. He may be more cautious than I gave him credit for."
// Answer Text :
"P71697861" "You expect me to believe that? You work together."
// Answer Text :
"P3074559196" "Regardless, I need the Antikythera back."
// Page Arachnos Text :
"P3013210657" "<color orange>Mako manages to roll his eyes, which looks especially odd given his facial structure.</color><br><br>Oh, for the love of- do you even <i><b>know</i></b> how Arachnos works, {HeroName}? We're all in one big game of King of the Mountain, here. Just because Recluse won doesn't mean the rest of us stopped playing.<br><br>Scorpion does his own thing, and I do mine. Sometimes we work together, sometimes we stab each other in the back. That's life in Arachnos. Heck, that's life in the <i>Isles</i>, but whatever. I can fix this.<br><br>You want the Antikythera, and I want the... ah, <i>exit strategy</i> you're offering if things go sour with Recluse. Can't predict that guy ever since his girlfriend came back from the dead."
// Answer Text :
"P1144069368" "What are you planning?"
// Page Attack Text :
"P3190107390" "<color orange>Mako grins, baring multiple rows of jagged teeth.</color><br><br>I can help you, {HeroName}. Ever since you and Harvan popped open Pandora's Box, Recluse has pretty much given up on that chase. He figures it's ok if he doesn't have Statesman's power, just as long as no one else does, either.<br><br>Meaning, you dropped pretty low on our hit list. No offense.<br><br>Anyway, it shouldn't be too big a deal for me to run a raid on Scorpion's stash. That sort of thing happens all the time, and to the other patrons, it'll just look like I'm trying to get it for myself. Meet me at these coordinates, and we'll open that tin can right up. Bet there's plenty of meat buried underneath all that metal...<br><br><color orange>Mako stares off in the general direction of Black Scorpion, hungrily. After a moment, his attention snaps back to the present.</color><br><br>Oh. And we'll get your Anty-ka-whatsit back too."
// Answer Text :
"P4203591568" "See you there."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - MakoMissionTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page TaskIncomplete Text :
"P8749061" "<color orange>There is a distinct predatory gleam in Mako's eye as he greets you.</color><br><br>Let's do this. I'm getting... <i>hungry</i>."
// Answer Text :
"P3008595171" "No way. I still don't trust you. I'm doing this alone."
// Answer Text :
"P1029490246" "Alright, come on, then."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P1057976488" "{HeroName}, I'm not sure what to do next. Arachnos controls every island in the Rogue Isles... they could be keeping it anywhere.<br><br><color orange>Harvan shrugs apologetically.</color><br><br>I'm afraid I'm no good in situations like these. What are you planning to do?"
// AcceptString :
"P4135297233" "Simple. I'll find Captain Mako, and beat the info out of him."
// SendOffString :
"P858245221" "<color orange>Harvan seems somewhat taken aback by your matter-of-fact tone.</color><br><br>Oh. I... I see. Well, I suppose that is one way to do it.<br><br>If that's what works, then I'm for it. Good luck, {HeroName}!"
// TaskSubTitle :
"P3144595053" "<color deepskyblue>Part Two: That Dangerous Game</color>"

